 Supported modes:
 
+* `proxy setup` installs the official Mihomo core and MetaCubeXD dashboard,
+  optionally imports a Clash/Mihomo YAML subscription, and enables managed mode
+* `proxy managed` starts Mihomo on demand and routes only the managed browser
+  through its loopback mixed proxy port
 * `proxy system` uses the Windows proxy configuration
 * `proxy off` forces direct connections
 * `proxy set` accepts Chromium proxy rules such as
@@ -105,6 +121,50 @@ Changing the proxy restarts the managed browser when it is already running.
 Proxy URLs containing embedded usernames or passwords are rejected because
 Chromium command-line proxy configuration does not support them.
 
+## Managed proxy
+
+Managed proxy runtime files live under `out/browserctl/mihomo` and are ignored
+by Git. This includes the downloaded Mihomo executable, MetaCubeXD files,
+subscriptions, generated configuration, logs, and process state. Subscription
+URLs and credentials are never added to the source repository.
+
+The managed profile is deliberately browser-only: listeners bind to loopback,
+LAN access and TUN mode are disabled, and Chromium connects to the local mixed
+HTTP/SOCKS port. Closing the managed browser also stops Mihomo. Direct and
+system proxy modes do not start the core.
+
+Core, dashboard, and URL-based subscription updates are checked at browser
+startup, at most once per configured interval (24 hours by default). Core
+downloads use the official GitHub release asset digest when available. Before
+replacement, the new executable and active configuration are tested; a failed
+upgrade restores the previous executable. Subscription changes also keep and
+restore the last known-good profile when validation or restart fails.
+
+The first version accepts complete Clash/Mihomo YAML subscriptions or local
+YAML files. Raw Base64 URI lists need conversion to Clash/Mihomo YAML before
+import.
+
+`proxy dashboard` opens the local CCCrome proxy settings page. It can import,
+refresh, or clear a subscription; update the core and dashboard; configure the
+automatic update interval; switch rule/global/direct mode; and select or test
+nodes. Its Advanced dashboard link opens the bundled MetaCubeXD traffic,
+connections, rules, and logs interface.
+
+Useful commands:
+
+```powershell
+.\ccchrome.cmd proxy setup <subscription-url>
+.\ccchrome.cmd proxy dashboard
+.\ccchrome.cmd proxy nodes
+.\ccchrome.cmd proxy select "PROXY" "Hong Kong 01"
+.\ccchrome.cmd proxy mode rule
+.\ccchrome.cmd proxy subscription update
+.\ccchrome.cmd proxy subscription clear
+.\ccchrome.cmd proxy core update
+.\ccchrome.cmd proxy auto-update on --interval-hours 24
+.\ccchrome.cmd proxy ports --mixed 7890 --controller 9090
+```
+
 ## Practical model
 
 * `open` creates a new tab when the DevTools helper endpoint is available
